course: dictionary
lesson: 9249
title: Many meanings of sorry
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several jobs. The words around it show you which job it has. «He lies awake feeling awful and says sorry at breakfast.» Here sorry means he feels bad about something he did wrong, and he says so.
explain: Sorry can also mean you feel sad for someone else. «I'm sorry your cat is ill» shows care, not guilt. Ask yourself: did someone do something wrong, or does someone feel for another person?
explain: Sorry is also a polite word. «Sorry?» means "please say that again, I didn't hear." «Sorry, excuse me» means "pardon me," as you squeeze past someone. Check by putting your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have it.
explain: Other places use sorry in their own ways. In China, when you bump into someone you say «duìbuqǐ (sorry, I did it)», and they answer «méi guānxi (never mind)». A good apology says what you did and how you will put it right.
fact: Sorry is an adjective (sorry, sorrier, sorriest) and an interjection (Sorry!).
fact: «Sorry» can mean you feel bad for doing wrong, or sad for someone else.
fact: «Sorry?» politely asks someone to say something again.
fact: «Sorry, excuse me» politely asks to pass someone.
fact: Common phrases: say sorry, feel sorry for, sorry about, sorry to hear, better safe than sorry.
exercise: «He lies awake feeling awful and says sorry at breakfast.» What does sorry mean here? | Happy to see his friends | Poor and sad-looking | Used to ask someone to repeat | *Feeling bad about something he did wrong
exercise: «Sorry, excuse me,» said Mia as she squeezed past the queue. What does sorry mean here? | *Politely asking to pass | Feeling sad for someone else | Feeling bad for doing wrong | Used to say you didn't hear
exercise: «The wet, muddy kitten was a sorry sight.» What does sorry mean in this sentence? | Used to say you didn't hear | Feeling bad for doing wrong | *Poor and sad-looking | Feeling sad for someone else
test: «I'm sorry your cat is ill.» What does sorry mean? | Used to say no politely | Feeling bad for doing wrong | *Feeling sad for someone else | Used to say you didn't hear
test: In China, after you say «duìbuqǐ (sorry, I did it)», the other person answers «méi guānxi». What does that answer mean? | Sorry, I did it | Thank you very much | *Never mind
exam: In which sentence does sorry mean the speaker did not hear? | I'm sorry I broke your pencil | It was a sorry sight after the storm | *«Sorry? Could you say that again?» | I'm sorry your dog is lost
